<title>ITALY: Italy's Ciampi questions tight stability pact.</title>
<headline>Italy's Ciampi questions tight stability pact.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said on Friday that rigid numerical criteria in a proposed stability pact for countries joining Europe's planned single currency would be dangerous.</p>
<p>Ciampi said earlier in a speech that Italy was fully in favour of the pact but added in response to reporters' questions: &quot;Personally, I believe that rigid numerical criteria would be dangerous&quot;.</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom +39 6 678 2505</p>
</text>
